<description>&lt;p&gt;Iraqi security forces arrested an Iraqi duo suspected of plotting a synagogue attack in Germany and foiled a smuggling attempt of 36,000 liters of crude oil in Kirkuk, while also detecting a pipeline breach there. Baghdad closed two border crossings in the Kurdistan region with Syria and Iran and ordered a nationwide deployment to secure oil fields, prompting protests by families of terrorism victims over benefit cuts in Mosul and job demands from petroleum engineering graduates in Kirkuk. President Al Zaidi called for dialogue and constitutional commitment as former US diplomat criticism of the Erbil-Baghdad dispute continued, and Trump backed Al Zaidi's authority. The UCDP recorded 396 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxPT2MxVEJYVHRnSDRQZzRETWUyMnlCYUJDTTVTVzNuenBwRkRKeTgxZnBDR0VUVWt4akRiYzdMSnc5Sk9PWTBUMy00UFNBeUxsU0F1T1dzcFM2QkFuYTJINzZ1WmJzYUxaZnJoM3U1Q1k3N1JjLXZyQ29TS3IwZ1EwQU0yaXVNcnk0Y3ZIWDFuSzlOekJjb0RyMzdBR1N6TXJITGtzM09PQ2s4Ujg?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Times of Israel&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxQVGIxMEpXQXE2YmM2ZFNJdG42Z3JuNHhsN3dFNXU5RURHUkhsUkRYRTBYQS1uZFpweGRIMm84MUE5b2Zjb19XNWhzQjhVNGJ5NmRrN1ZPbEVGX0k2cTlTZ01lRWJJN3FiWENfZ3VRSFhPT0tsbW9GQzFIX04xRDYxQXgzU25ybS1tUVhWbUJobUotVFA5RVBzLWJzTHJGRlNMS1Q5RmluSEV6b0pLa2NObg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kurdistan24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxQQ29fanpKUlAySEktXzNRN0hfRy1zbG5USXdDdmZXVkpZcV9XOEx2ZnVqemlzWnloVkt5dHRhLWpRcnJPRjhhckVETmFkcFlDUU9xV2ltME1MLTJFVGQ0UnFTOUoweTYtMHAwY0R2RFh2aldTanNELUVvaXFWTEZBM0VzSTV3Q01CSDczSFpraw?oc=5&quot;&gt;شفق نيوز&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiVE